  "term": "fast muscle fiber",
  "definition": "A fast muscle fiber is a type of muscle fiber distinguished from slow muscle fibers when researchers examine muscle fiber composition. In the source, having fewer fast fibers in the soleus muscle was associated with reduced muscle strength and age-related motor activity problems.",
